### Planner Response

I have resolved the issue with the `REP-XXXXXXXXXX_Audit_Pack.xlsx` files in your project root!

---

### What Was Happening:
When unit tests (`pytest`) ran in the background or reports were exported without specifying an output directory, the reporting engine ([report_engine.py](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/src/reporting/report_engine.py)) defaulted to saving generated Excel audit packs (`REP-*.xlsx`) directly into your source code root folder (`FinAuditPro/`). This cluttered your project file tree in VS Code / Finder.

---

### Changes Implemented:

1. **Isolated Output Directory**:
   - Updated [report_engine.py](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/src/reporting/report_engine.py) so that generated audit packs automatically route to a dedicated `data/reports/` directory instead of dumping into the root folder.
   - Added automatic directory creation (`os.makedirs("data/reports", exist_ok=True)`).

2. **Isolated Test Execution**:
   - Updated [test_reporting.py](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/tests/test_reporting.py) and [test_fatal_fixes.py](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/tests/test_fatal_fixes.py) to use isolated temporary memory directories (`tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()`).
   - Running `pytest` will **never** generate temporary report files in your project workspace tree again.

3. **Workspace Cleanup**:
   - Purged all leftover `REP-*.xlsx` files from the root folder.
   - Verified that all 52 test suites pass with 100% success rate.
