### Engineering & Security Hardening (Phase 2) Completed

All remaining security and UX gaps identified in [FinAuditPro_Engineering_Audit.md](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/FinAuditPro_Engineering_Audit.md) (§5.2, §5.6, §5.7, §7) have been resolved, verified, and pushed to `origin/main`.

---

### Phase 2 Hardening Deliverables

1. **Systemic AI Prompt Injection Defense**
   - Implemented a unified `_sanitize_and_wrap_context` helper in [prompt_engine.py](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/src/ai/prompt_engine.py).
   - Applied untrusted content tag wrapping (`<untrusted_..._data>`) and explicit anti-prompt-injection system instructions across **all 8 prompt builders**, protecting the AI Copilot from document jailbreaks or finding manipulation.

2. **PBKDF2 Password Hashing Minimum Floor**
   - Updated [auth.py](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/src/security/auth.py) to enforce a strict **100,000 iteration minimum floor** (`MINIMUM_ITERATIONS = 100_000`) in `PasswordHasher.get_iterations()`, preventing weak hash downgrades via environment variables.

3. **Magic Byte Document Content Sniffing**
   - Enhanced [document_validator.py](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/src/document_intelligence/document_validator.py) with magic header content sniffing (`%PDF-`, `\x89PNG`, `\xff\xd8\xff`, `PK\x03\x04`). Files with mismatched signatures are immediately rejected to prevent extension spoofing.

4. **UI Wire-Up for Disaster Recovery & Backup Restoration**
   - Added a dedicated **"Restore Database Backup"** action button in [settings.py](file:///Users/aryanyadav/Desktop/PROJECTS/Audit/src/ui/settings.py).
   - Connected file selection and confirmation dialogs to `BackupEngine().restore_backup()`, completing the disaster recovery lifecycle.

---

